.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-GET-OBJECT-COUNT 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-get-object-count \- return the number of objects in a bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm get-object-count
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I ERN
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-p\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns the number of objects in a bucket, optionally filtered by
object key prefix.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only count objects whose key starts with this prefix. Optional; if
omitted, every object in the bucket is counted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A summary
.RI ( "{ern, count}" )
is printed as JSON, where
.I count
is the number of matching objects.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no
bucket with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
Count every object in a bucket:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm get-object-count \e
    --bucket ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports
.fi
.RE
.PP
Count only objects under a given key prefix:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm get-object-count \e
    --bucket ern:euclid:storage:eu-central-1:000000000000:bucket:reports \e
    --prefix 2025/
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-size (1),
